+---
+id: task-001-fix-sku-case-free-shipping-threshold-vat-rounding
+type: task
+title: "Fix SKU case, free-shipping threshold, VAT rounding"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+# Request
+
+Three reports against the order service, fixed to match the README business rules:
+
+1. Lower-case SKUs (e.g. `lb-220`) were refused as unknown: `Catalog.find` now looks up the canonical (trimmed, upper-case) SKU.
+2. Free shipping at exactly €50.00 was not applied: `shippingCost` now uses `>=` the threshold.
+3. Line VAT was rounded down (€1.99 at 22% gave €0.43): `lineVat` now rounds half up via `percentOf` (gives €0.44).
+
+Tests added in `test/orders.test.ts` for each; `npm test` passes.
diff --git a/src/catalog.ts b/src/catalog.ts
